    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0058_07a7daa9cbe6.png\" style=\"width: 515px; height: 106px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0058_2d618170c1f8.png\" style=\"width: 404px; height: 121px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0058_8f27b0f9703a.png\" style=\"width: 482px; height: 138px;\" /></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0058_317239654f9c.png\" style=\"width: 414px; height: 257px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p>We know that drugs help us diagnose and cure numerous illnesses. But any drug consumed by humans can actually have two kinds of effects - therapeutic effects and side effects. The goal is to prescribe the ideal drug, the one that only has a therapeutic effect.</p>"
